A||||4||BOILERMAKER||Door Dew strips||||5
Z||000000||BOILERMAKER||09-22-1999||12:24 PM||||I'm getting ready to replace the outer dew wipes for both doors and was wondering how tough this was.  I know the Michigan Fiero Website has instructions, but these seem a little confusing towards the end.  I was wondering how many screws hold this puppy on and if anyone has done this before.<P>Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||mwbackus||09-22-1999||02:10 PM||||I have.. there are really only two screws which pose a problem.  My method is to simply pry the old strip from these screws with a flat blade screwdrive.  (The metal the the dew strip is made from is comparable to tin foil.)  After this, the already loose screws can easily be backed out with a pair of needle nose pliers.  Be sure to replace the screws from hell with some short hex head units.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||09-22-1999||05:46 PM||||Rodney Dickman sells a tool for replacing the dew strips for $7.50 plus $1.50 shipping and handling.  I was thinking of ordering one.  You can see it by going to the Fiero Secrets web site.||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||09-22-1999||09:34 PM||||Now there's a job that I need to do on all 3 of my Fieros, but I keep putting it off. It just looked like it was going to be one of those time consuming all afternoon jobs. I suppoese I'd better buy some and do the dew. They are old, brittle and cracked--kind of like me.||||reg||1
Z||000004||DJRice||09-23-1999||08:57 AM||||This board is absolutely amazing!  I logged on this morning with the intention of posting this exact question.  Instead, I just log on and read the answer to the question I didnt even have to post!<P>Do you still have to remove the window from the door?????  I remember looking at the door with the intent of replacing the strips, but changed my mind with the quickness because it looked like I was going to have to completely  dismantle the door.||||reg||7
